# Release-critical markdown: prettier rewrites `[comment]: <> (START OF GITHUB README)`
# into `[comment]: <> 'START OF GITHUB README'`, and `make build` slices the published
# npm/README.md between exactly those markers. `.prettierrc` also sets useTabs, so prettier
# re-tabs the fenced code blocks that markdownlint's MD010 de-tabs, and .husky/pre-commit
# runs `prettier -w` before `pre-commit run` -- the two rewrite the same file in opposite
# directions on every commit that touches it. Both root files are copies of src/README.md
# and src/RELEASE.md (src/package.json "postbuild"), and src/ is ignored below, so
# formatting them here only creates drift the next build overwrites. markdownlint-cli2
# (pre-commit) owns the markdown style instead.
README.md
RELEASE.md
